course: dictionary
lesson: 4872
title: ID: proving who you are
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: ID is a short word, and it is short for identification. Identification means showing who someone is. Most people write it in capitals: ID. Read the words around it: «Please show your ID at the door.» The words show and door tell you that ID is something you hand over to prove who you are.
explain: ID has another meaning too. «Each player has a user ID, so the game can find their score.» Here an ID is a number or name that identifies something. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Try "a name or number that tells who or what it is" and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Words can change meaning in different subjects. In a computer game, a user ID is a code that belongs to one player. In psychology, which is the study of the mind, the id is a grown-up word for the part of the mind with basic wishes and instincts. When you meet ID, look at the topic and the clues in the sentence.
fact: ID is short for identification.
fact: An ID is a card or document that shows who you are, like a passport or a student card.
fact: «Photo ID» is an ID that has a picture of you on it.
fact: A user ID or product ID is a number or name that identifies one user or one thing.
fact: In psychology, "the id" means the part of the mind with basic wishes and instincts.
exercise: «Please show your ID at the door.» What is an ID here? | A flower that grows in gardens | *A card or paper that shows who you are | A loud noise | A type of bicycle
exercise: «Each player has a user ID, so the game can find their score.» What does a user ID do? | It is a holiday for players | It stops the screen from working | *It is a number or name that identifies one player | It makes the game louder
exercise: ID is short for which word? | *Identification | Iguana | Idea | Idle
test: «Every pupil at our school wears an ID badge on a string.» What is the ID badge for? | To keep the pupil warm | *To show who the pupil is | To tell the time | To make the badge look nice
test: In psychology, what is "the id"? | A kind of lamp | *The part of the mind with basic wishes and instincts | A type of cloud | A school subject
exam: Which sentence uses ID to mean a number or name that identifies something? | *«Enter your user ID to log in.» | «Bring your student ID to the library.» | «The ID card was in her bag.» | «Please show your ID at the bank.»
